<div class="body">
<h1>Elections</h1>
<div class="summary"><div class="jodit-content"><style> /* PAGE CONTAINER */ .page-container {     max-width: 1100px;     margin: auto;     padding: 20px;     font-family: Arial, sans-serif;     line-height: 1.6; }  /* BANNER */ .banner {     background-color: #003366;     color: #ffffff;     padding: 35px 20px;     text-align: center;     margin-bottom: 30px; }  .banner h1 {     margin: 0;     font-size: 34px; }  .banner p {     margin-top: 8px;     font-size: 16px; }  /* SECTION BOX */ .section-box {     background-color: #ffffff;     padding: 25px;     margin-bottom: 25px;     border-radius: 6px;     box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); }  /* HEADINGS */ .section-box h2 {     margin-top: 0;     color: #003366;     border-bottom: 2px solid #e6e6e6;     padding-bottom: 10px; }  /* LIST */ ul {     padding-left: 20px; }  li {     margin-bottom: 10px; }  /* LINK */ a {     color: #003366;     text-decoration: none; }  a:hover {     text-decoration: underline; }</style>  <div class="page-container"><!-- KEY INFORMATION -->     <div class="section-box">         <h2><span style="font-size: 24px;">November 3, 2026, General Municipal Election</span></h2>         <p style="text-align: justify;">The City&#8217;s General Municipal Election will be held on
Tuesday, November 3, 2026.</p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Canyon Lake 4-Day Vote Center</strong></p><p><span>Canyon Lake City Hall will serve as a </span><span>4-day Vote Center</span><span> for the November 3, 2026, General Election.</span></p><p><span>Location:</span><span> Canyon Lake City Hall,&nbsp;</span><span>31516 Railroad Canyon Road, Canyon Lake, CA 92587</span></p><p><span>Voting Dates and Hours:</span></p><p><strong><span>Saturday, October 31 &#8211; Monday, November 2</span></strong><br><span>9:00 a.m. &#8211; 5:00 p.m. daily</span></p><p><strong><span>Tuesday, November 3 (Election Day)</span></strong><br><span>7:00 a.m. &#8211; 8:00 p.m.</span></p><p><span>Voters can drop off their ballots at City Hall during normal business
hours beginning October 5, 2026, through November 2, 2026, from 8:00 a.m. to
5:00 p.m., Monday through Thursday, and on Election Day, November 3, 2026, from
7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>What's on the Local Ballot?</strong></p>

<p style="text-align: justify;">Canyon Lake voters will consider two City Council seats and one local
ballot measure.</p>

<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>City Council </strong></p>

<p style="text-align: justify;">Two City Council seats will be up for election for full four-year
terms.<span>&nbsp; </span>The candidates, listed in ballot
order, are: </p>

<p style="line-height: 0.5; text-align: justify;">Paul Kakis</p>
<p style="line-height: 0.5; text-align: justify;">Monica Lyons</p>
<p style="line-height: 0.5; text-align: justify;">Jeremy Smith</p>

<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Measure E</strong></p><p style="text-align: justify;">If approved by voters, Measure E, the <strong>Canyon Lake Public Safety and
Emergency Response Protection Measure</strong>, will establish a 1% local sales tax
(one cent per dollar), estimated to generate approximately $1.14 million
annually.<span>&nbsp; </span><span>&nbsp;</span>Revenue generated by Measure E would be
restricted to public safety and emergency response purposes and locally
controlled.</p>

<p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Additional Ballot information</strong></p>

<p style="text-align: justify;">For information about additional offices and measures appearing on the
November 3, 2026, ballot, visit the Riverside County Registrar of Voters
website at <a href="https://voteinfo.net/"><u>https://voteinfo.net/</u></a>.</p><p style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Make a Plan to Vote - Vote Early!</strong></p><ul><li style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Registered to Vote?&nbsp;</strong><span>The
last day to register to vote online for the November 3, 2026, General Election
is October 19.<span>&nbsp; </span>Visit <u><a href="https://registertovote.ca.gov/" target="_blank">https://registertovote.ca.gov/</a></u>.</span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span><strong>Return your ballot.&nbsp;</strong><span>County
elections officials will begin mailing ballots by October 5.<span>&nbsp; </span>Ballots can be dropped off at a drop-off
location, county elections office, or returned by mail after this date.</span></span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span><span><strong>Skip the lines on Election Day.&nbsp;</strong><span>The
first vote centers open for early in-person voting in all Voter&#8217;s Choice Act
counties on October 24. In-person early voting locations throughout California
will be open on Saturday, October 31.</span></span></span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span><span><span><strong>Get a postmark:&nbsp;</strong><span>Mail
your ballot early - mailed ballots must be postmarked on or before November 3.<span>&nbsp; </span><strong><em>Tip: </em></strong><span>&nbsp;</span>Get a manual postmark from a postal employee
inside a United States Post Office.</span></span></span></span></li><li style="text-align: justify;"><span><span><span><span><strong>Election Day.&nbsp;</strong><strong><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></strong><span>November
3 is the last day to vote in person or return a ballot. <span>&nbsp;</span>Polls are open from 7:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. for
in-person voting and ballot drop-off.</span></span></span></span></span></li></ul><h2><span style="font-size: 24px;">General Information</span></h2>         The City of Canyon Lake is a General Law city governed by a five-member City Council.              Members of the City Council serve staggered terms, with either two or three seats open              for election every two years.<p style="text-align: justify;">       The City Clerk serves as the Elections Officer and is responsible for the issuance and              acceptance of nomination papers and is the official Filing Officer for campaign statements.         </p>         <p style="text-align: justify;">             The City consolidates its election activities with the <a href="https://voteinfo.net/" target="_blank">County of Riverside</a>, which provides              voter registration, ballot materials, vote centers and other critical election functions.</p><p style="text-align: center;"> &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<a href="https://portal.laserfiche.com/Portal/Browse.aspx?id=70803&amp;repo=r-1cacdf5c" target="_blank"><img src="/vertical/Sites/%7B914485A7-E93B-4BFA-A369-593050FBB784%7D/uploads/Campaign_Filings_Button.jpg" width="163" height="163"></a><span>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<a href="https://voteinfo.net/" target="_blank"><img src="/vertical/Sites/%7B914485A7-E93B-4BFA-A369-593050FBB784%7D/uploads/ROV_Button.jpg" width="162" height="162"></a></span></p>     </div>  </div><p>&nbsp;<br></p></div></div>
</div>
